// BELLEST.QS0 - a Bell state, verified through the Hamiltonian estimator.
//
// Demonstrates: the ESTIMATE operator, expectation values, entanglement.
//
// Qubit-level explanation:
//   H 0 creates (|00>+|10>)/sqrt2; CNOT 0 1 turns it into the Bell state
//   (|00>+|11>)/sqrt2 on qubits 0 and 1. For this state the two-qubit
//   correlators are:
//       <Z0 Z1> =  1     (Z measurements of the two qubits always agree)
//       <X0 X1> =  1     (the same holds in the X basis)
//       <Y0 Y1> = -1     (but they are opposite in the Y basis)
//   That pattern is the signature of a maximally entangled pair: it cannot
//   be produced by any product state.
//
//   ESTIMATE evaluates a weighted sum of Pauli expectations directly from
//   the amplitudes, with no sampling, so each estimate[i] is exact up to f64
//   rounding:
//       estimate[0] = 1.0*<Z0 Z1> =  1.0
//       estimate[1] = 1.0*<X0 X1> =  1.0
//       estimate[2] = 1.0*<Y0 Y1> = -1.0
//   Combining them gives a Hamiltonian expectation such as
//   <Z0Z1> + <X0X1> - <Y0Y1> = 3, the maximal violation value for a Bell
//   inequality.
//
// Run:
//   plasma run examples/BELLEST.QS0
//   plasma run examples/BELLEST.QS0 --gpu
QUBITS 2
H 0
CNOT 0 1
ESTIMATE 1.0 Z0Z1
ESTIMATE 1.0 X0X1
ESTIMATE 1.0 Y0Y1
PRINT
END